    <string-array name="steps_samsung">
        <item>Settings → Apps → DT → Battery → Unrestricted.</item>
        <item>Settings → Battery → Background usage limits: keep DT out of Sleeping apps and Deep sleeping apps.</item>
        <item>An unrestricted app is never put to sleep, so “Put unused apps to sleep” can stay on.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_xiaomi">
        <item>Settings → Apps → Manage apps → DT → Autostart: on.</item>
        <item>Same page → Battery saver → No restrictions.</item>
        <item>Recent apps: long-press DT and tap the lock so it is not cleared.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_oppo">
        <item>Settings → Apps → App management → DT → Battery usage: allow background activity and auto launch.</item>
        <item>Settings → Battery → More settings: turn off optimisation for DT.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_vivo">
        <item>Settings → Battery → Background power consumption management → DT: allow.</item>
        <item>i Manager → App manager → Autostart manager → DT: on.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_oneplus">
        <item>Settings → Apps → DT → Battery → Unrestricted (or “Don’t optimise”).</item>
        <item>Settings → Battery → Advanced: turn off adaptive and sleep standby optimisation if reminders arrive late.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_huawei">
        <item>Settings → Battery → App launch → DT: switch to manage manually and allow all three options.</item>
        <item>Settings → Apps → DT → Battery: allow running in the background.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_transsion">
        <item>Phone Master → App management → Auto-start: allow DT.</item>
        <item>Settings → Battery → App power saving → DT: no restrictions.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="steps_generic">
        <item>Settings → Apps → DT → Battery: Unrestricted (or “Don’t optimise”).</item>
        <item>If the phone has an autostart or background-launch list, allow DT there.</item>
    </string-array>
